from tn import *
def C(ch,*a,**k): TN(10,"science",ch,*a,**k)
C("genetics","Asha looked at her father's dimples and her own. \"Traits pass from parents to children,\" said her teacher.",
 ["Gregor Johann Mendel is called the Father of Genetics. From his experiments with pea plants he explained inheritance. A monohybrid cross follows one pair of contrasting traits and a dihybrid cross follows two. Mendel's laws include the law of dominance, the law of segregation and the law of independent assortment.",
  "Chromosomes carry DNA, and a chromosome has a centromere and chromatids. They are autosomes and sex chromosomes, and a karyotype is the picture of the chromosome set. DNA has the double helix structure described by Watson and Crick, and it replicates before cell division.",
  "In humans sex is determined by the sex chromosomes: females are XX and males are XY. A mutation is a sudden change in the genetic material."],
 ["Mendel","monohybrid cross","dominance","chromosome","DNA","sex determination"],
 ("In a cross of Tt x Tt, what is the ratio of tall to short?",["Tall is dominant.","The offspring are TT, Tt, Tt and tt.","So tall : short is 3 : 1."]),
 ("Mendel worked on fruit flies.",["Mendel used pea plants.","Fruit flies were used later by Morgan."]),
 ["Mendel is the Father of Genetics.","Monohybrid ratio is 3 : 1.","DNA has a double helix.","XX is female and XY is male."],
 ["m|The Father of Genetics is|Mendel|Darwin|Watson|He crossed pea plants.","t|DNA has a double helix structure.|T|Watson and Crick.","m|Human females have the chromosomes|XX|XY|YY|Males are XY.","t|A monohybrid cross follows one trait.|T|Yes.","m|The phenotypic ratio of a monohybrid cross is|3 : 1|1 : 1|9 : 3|Dominant to recessive.","s|What is a sudden change in genes called?|mutation|Mutation.","m|A picture of the chromosome set is a|karyotype|diagram|graph|Used in diagnosis.","t|DNA replicates before cell division.|T|Yes."])
C("origin-and-evolution-of-life","Raju saw a fossil of a shell in a museum. \"That shows life of long ago,\" said his teacher.",
 ["Life on Earth began about 3.5 to 4 billion years ago. Evidences for evolution come from fossils, comparative anatomy and embryology. Lamarck's theory said that organs used more are developed and passed on, while Darwin's theory of natural selection said that the fittest organisms in a changing environment survive.",
  "Variation is the difference among individuals of the same species, and it is the raw material for natural selection. Palaeobotany is the study of fossil plants, and fossilisation is how remains are preserved in rocks, whose age can be found by radioactive dating.",
  "Ethnobotany studies how people use plants, and astrobiology or exobiology looks for life beyond Earth."],
 ["fossil","Lamarckism","Darwinism","natural selection","variation","astrobiology"],
 ("Who proposed natural selection?",["It explains survival of the fittest.","It was proposed by a British naturalist.","Charles Darwin."]),
 ("Lamarck proposed natural selection.",["Natural selection is Darwin's theory.","Lamarck proposed use and disuse."]),
 ["Fossils show earlier life.","Darwin: natural selection.","Variation is needed for selection.","Astrobiology looks for life in space."],
 ["m|Natural selection was proposed by|Darwin|Lamarck|Mendel|Survival of the fittest.","t|Fossils are evidence of evolution.|T|Yes.","m|Study of fossil plants is|palaeobotany|ethnobotany|zoology|Ancient plants.","t|Lamarck gave the theory of use and disuse.|T|Yes.","m|Differences among individuals are|variation|fossils|genes only|Needed for selection.","s|What is the study of life beyond Earth?|astrobiology;exobiology|Astrobiology.","m|Age of rocks can be found using|radioactive dating|a ruler|a magnet|Isotopes decay.","t|Ethnobotany is the study of how people use plants.|T|Yes."])
C("breeding-and-biotechnology","Meena's uncle grew a high-yielding rice variety. \"Plant breeding did this,\" he said.",
 ["The Green Revolution raised food grain production using high-yielding varieties, fertilisers and irrigation. Plant breeding develops better crops by methods such as introduction, selection, polyploidy breeding, mutation breeding and hybridisation. They aim for high yield, better quality and resistance to disease and pests.",
  "Animal breeding includes inbreeding, which mates closely related animals, outbreeding, which mates unrelated ones, and heterosis, the extra vigour of hybrids.",
  "Genetic engineering changes the genes of an organism and uses techniques like gene cloning. Biotechnology is used in medicine to make insulin and vaccines, stem cells can grow into different cell types, DNA fingerprinting identifies people, and genetically modified crops carry added genes."],
 ["Green Revolution","hybridisation","heterosis","genetic engineering","stem cells","DNA fingerprinting"],
 ("What is a hybrid?",["Hybridisation crosses two varieties.","The offspring combine their traits.","The offspring is a hybrid."]),
 ("DNA fingerprinting is used to cook food.",["DNA fingerprinting identifies individuals.","It is used in crime and parentage tests."]),
 ["Plant breeding improves crops.","Heterosis is hybrid vigour.","Genetic engineering changes genes.","Stem cells can become many cell types."],
 ["m|The Green Revolution increased|food grain production|rainfall|forests|It used high-yielding varieties.","t|Hybridisation crosses different varieties.|T|Yes.","m|DNA fingerprinting is used to|identify individuals|dye cloth|clean water|In crime and parentage.","t|Stem cells cannot divide.|F|They divide and form many types.","m|Hybrid vigour is called|heterosis|inbreeding|mutation|Better than parents.","s|What is mating closely related animals called?|inbreeding|Inbreeding.","m|Insulin can be made by|genetic engineering|ploughing|distillation|Using bacteria.","t|GM crops carry added genes.|T|Yes."])
C("health-and-diseases","In school Asha attended a health talk. \"Healthy habits protect us from harm,\" said the counsellor.",
 ["Health means being well in body, mind and society. This chapter explains abuse and how to protect oneself: any harm to a child by an adult is abuse, and children should know safe and unsafe behaviour, trust a parent or teacher, and report to the helpline when something is wrong.",
  "Drug abuse is the wrong use of drugs, alcohol and tobacco. It leads to dependence, behavioural changes and harm to the body. Tobacco smoking causes lung disease and cancer. Alcohol harms the liver and the brain. De-addiction and rehabilitation measures with medical help and family support help people recover.",
  "The chapter also lists common diseases and their prevention, and stresses healthy habits like clean food, exercise and avoiding addictive substances."],
 ["health","abuse","drug dependence","tobacco hazards","alcohol harm","rehabilitation"],
 ("Whom can a child tell if someone makes them feel unsafe?",["Children need trusted adults.","A parent, a teacher or a helpline can help.","So tell a trusted adult at once."]),
 ("Smoking is harmless in small amounts.",["Tobacco harms the lungs and heart.","No amount is safe."]),
 ["Health covers body, mind and society.","Tell a trusted adult if unsafe.","Tobacco and alcohol harm the body.","Rehabilitation helps recovery."],
 ["m|Tobacco use mainly harms the|lungs|toes|hair only|It causes cancer.","t|Children should tell a trusted adult about unsafe behaviour.|T|Yes.","m|Wrong use of drugs is|drug abuse|exercise|diet|It leads to dependence.","t|Alcohol harms the liver.|T|Yes.","m|Help to recover from addiction is|rehabilitation|abuse|infection|With support.","s|What can children do if they feel unsafe? Say tell a ___.|trusted adult|Tell a trusted adult.","m|Good health includes|body, mind and social wellbeing|only exercise|only food|All three.","t|De-addiction needs medical and family support.|T|Yes."])
C("environmental-management","Raju's class planted trees and saved water. \"Small steps manage the environment,\" said his teacher.",
 ["Conservation is the careful use of natural resources. Forests are important for oxygen, rain, soil protection and wildlife, but deforestation, the clearing of forests, harms them, so forests must be conserved. Wildlife is declining due to habitat loss, and organisations and laws aim to protect species.",
  "Soil erosion is the removal of top soil by wind and water, and it can be managed by planting trees and terracing. Resources are renewable like sunlight and wind, or non-renewable like coal and petroleum, which are fossil fuels that must be conserved.",
  "Non-conventional energy sources such as solar energy, biogas and shale gas offer cleaner choices."],
 ["conservation","deforestation","wildlife","soil erosion","fossil fuels","solar energy"],
 ("Name two renewable energy sources.",["Renewable sources do not run out.","Sunlight gives solar energy.","Biogas is also renewable."]),
 ("Coal is a renewable resource.",["Coal takes millions of years to form.","So it is non-renewable."]),
 ["Conserve forests and wildlife.","Soil erosion removes top soil.","Fossil fuels are non-renewable.","Solar energy and biogas are cleaner."],
 ["m|Clearing of forests is|deforestation|afforestation|erosion|It harms the environment.","t|Coal is a fossil fuel.|T|Yes.","m|A renewable source of energy is|solar energy|petroleum|coal|Sunlight does not end.","t|Soil erosion adds nutrients to soil.|F|It removes top soil.","m|Planting trees helps to|prevent soil erosion|cause pollution|dry rivers|Roots hold soil.","s|What gas can be made from cattle dung for fuel?|biogas|Biogas.","m|Careful use of resources is|conservation|waste|erosion|Saves for the future.","t|Wildlife needs protection.|T|Yes."])
